# debug.keystore is intentionally NOT ignored: it is committed at the repo root so every build
# (CI or local) signs debug APKs with the same certificate. A debug keystore carries no real
# secret (it's never used for release/Play Store signing) -- committing it is standard practice,
# and it's what prevents "package conflicts with the current package" install errors caused by
# each build environment generating its own random debug certificate.
